learnings:
  - 'The calibration moat is now MEASURED not asserted: gradeFabric populates real confidence from survive/overturn on the live ledger. computePickId must EXCLUDE calibratedConfidence (graded-later metadata ≠ event identity) so grading doesn''t break the content-address'
  - 'The multi-writer corruption surfaces are all fail-closed now: binary→conflict, oversized→conflict, 3rd-gen-merge-onto-a-merge-strand→unsealed. The merge engine never silently produces wrong bytes'
