body: |-
  GRADER (#grade, 0e3d3d57) — Loid's moat made real: admit seeds calibratedConfidence from the gate rule (linked 0.9/independent 0.6/FAST_ADMIT 0.8); gradeFabric grades it against OUTCOME like the classroom certify→outcome loop — a strand's authored symbols (born ∪ contractChanged) are OVERTURNED when a later strand retires one or a #resolve contends it (confidence ↓), SURVIVED when they hold across a window (↑), PENDING when too recent. applyGrades mutates calibratedConfidence in the ledger + appends the trajectory to .warpline/grades.jsonl (gitignored) under #fabric-lock. KEY DESIGN: computePickId now EXCLUDES calibratedConfidence — it's graded-later metadata, not event identity, so grading can update it without changing the content-address. BACKFILL on the live fabric: 4 survived→0.8, 1 overturned→0.68 (the v2 commit, 2/37 symbols reworked by v3 + the lock fix), 2 pending. 80% pick-class survival. The linked-vs-independent PRIOR experiment awaits multi-writer admits (all 8 strands are auto-seal picks) — reported honestly.

  HARDENING (a7acfac1) — the Reviewer's dogfood-blockers, each now fails CLOSED:
  - H3 binary: computeMerge reads RAW BYTES (gitShowBuffer, no UTF-8 decode); MergePlan.files is Buffer-valued. A binary blob (NUL) changed on both sides → hard conflict, never a text-merge corruption.
  - H1 3rd-gen merge: a merge strand's provenance.gitCommit is ONE parent and lacks the merged bytes, so re-basing a later merge's base/theirs off it mis-materializes. Merge strands are now MARKED (strand.merged); admit's CLEAN path refuses to materialize onto a merge strand → fail-closed unsealed. Proven with a 3-agent test (A fast, B clean-merge marked, C re-bases onto the merge → CLEAN but sealed:false).
  - M1: merge3 caps the O(n·m) LCS grid at 4M cells → oversized/minified file fails closed (whole-file conflict), no OOM.

  REMAINING hardening (T-2026-06-27-002): H2 rename (changedPaths lacks -M), mode-change detection, and the rest of the G-test matrix (G1 interleaved 3+ agents, G3 KNOT-downgrade, G4 multi-file).

  This continues the audit-redirect (TD-2026-06-27-798): the moat + the fail-closed safety are the priorities, per the team; per-domain CAS stays deferred. The full git-replacement multi-writer path is now: decide → materialize → resolve → (concurrency-safe via #fabric-lock) → (fails closed on the corruption cases) → (confidence graded against outcome).</parameter>
